#. TRANSLATOR: %%SETTINGS%% is the MX Updater Settings label in MX Tools and the System Menu; %%PREFERENCES%% is the Preferences entry in the right-click menu; keep both exactly as written
#: help.md:7
msgid ""
"MX Updater monitors your MX Linux system for available package updates and "
"shows a tray icon reflecting the current status. Desktop notifications can "
"also be shown when updates become available. Personal preferences can be "
"adjusted by opening %%SETTINGS%% from MX Tools, the System Menu, or "
"%%PREFERENCES%% from the right-click menu of the tray icon."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:17
msgid "Controls the upgrade method and schedule:"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%FULL%% is the "full" upgrade mode label in the settings
#: help.md:21
msgid ""
"%%FULL%% -- upgrades packages and allows installing or removing packages "
"where needed to satisfy dependencies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%BASIC%% is the "basic" upgrade mode label in the settings
#: help.md:25
msgid ""
"%%BASIC%% -- upgrades packages but will not install new ones or remove "
"existing ones. Safer, but some packages may be kept back."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%NALA%% is the name of the package manager "Nala"; do not translate it. The word "Nala" in the description is also a proper name and should not be translated.
#: help.md:29
msgid ""
"%%NALA%% -- when checked, uses Nala instead of apt as the package manager "
"(only shown if Nala is installed)."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%REFRESH%% is the refresh interval dropdown label; %%AUTOMATIC_UPGRADE%% is the automatic upgrade checkbox label
#: help.md:34
msgid ""
"The %%REFRESH%% dropdown sets how often the package list is fetched from "
"the servers (daily, every 3 days, weekly, every 2 weeks, monthly, or "
"never). The %%AUTOMATIC_UPGRADE%% checkbox enables unattended upgrades on "
"the same schedule."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:41
msgid ""
"Choose what happens when you left-click the tray icon. Available choices "
"depend on which applications are installed:"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%VIEW_AND_UPGRADE%% is the "View and Upgrade" left-click mode label
#: help.md:46
msgid ""
"%%VIEW_AND_UPGRADE%% -- opens the MX Updater upgrade window when updates "
"are available; falls back to the first installed package manager otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%SYNAPTIC%% is the name of the package manager "Synaptic"; do not translate it
#: help.md:50
msgid ""
"%%SYNAPTIC%% -- opens Synaptic Package Manager (always, with or without "
"updates)."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%MX_PKG_INSTALLER%% is the application name; keep it exactly as written
#: help.md:55
msgid ""
"%%MX_PKG_INSTALLER%% -- opens MX Package Installer (always, with or without "
"updates)."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:57
msgid ""
"Middle-clicking the tray icon always opens MX Package Installer, regardless "
"of the left-click setting."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:59
msgid "Right-Click Menu"
msgstr ""

#: help.md:61
msgid ""
"Right-clicking the tray icon opens the context menu. Entries are only shown "
"when the corresponding application is installed or condition applies:"
msgstr ""

#: help.md:65
msgid ""
"%%VIEW_AND_UPGRADE%% -- open the upgrade window (shown when updates are "
"available)."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:68
msgid "%%SYNAPTIC%% -- open Synaptic Package Manager."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:72
msgid "%%MX_PKG_INSTALLER%% -- open MX Package Installer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%MX_REPO_MANAGER%% is the application name "MX Repo Manager"; keep it exactly as written
#: help.md:77
msgid "%%MX_REPO_MANAGER%% -- open MX Repo Manager."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:80
msgid ""
"%%CHECK_FOR_UPDATES%% -- open a terminal and fetch the latest package lists "
"from the servers."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:83
msgid ""
"%%HISTORY%% -- open MX Updater History to view recently installed or "
"removed packages."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:86
msgid "%%AUTO_UPDATE_LOGS%% -- view the log of automatic upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:89
msgid "%%AUTO_UPDATE_DPKG_LOGS%% -- view the dpkg log of automatic upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:92
msgid "%%PREFERENCES%% -- open the MX Updater Preferences window."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:95
msgid "%%ABOUT%% -- version information, license and changelog."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:98
msgid ""
"%%RESTART_MX_UPDATER%% -- restart the tray icon process. Useful after "
"manual configuration changes; will show a notification if updates are "
"available."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:101
msgid ""
"%%HIDE_WHEN_NO_UPDATES%% -- only shown when the system is up to date; "
"toggles whether the tray icon is hidden when there are no updates (not "
"available on KDE)."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:104
msgid "%%QUIT%% -- close MX Updater."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:109
msgid ""
"Choose the icon set used in the system tray. Each set shows two icons: the "
"left icon is used when updates are available, the right icon when the "
"system is up to date."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:113
msgid ""
"Note: with %%BASIC_UPGRADE%% selected, packages that would require "
"installing or removing other packages are kept back. When all remaining "
"updates are such kept-back packages the up-to-date (right) icon is shown."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:118
msgid ""
"The %%TRANSPARENT_WIREFRAME%% toggle makes the no-updates icon transparent "
"with either black or white wire lines. Use black wires on a light panel, "
"white wires on a dark panel, so the icon does not disappear into the panel "
"background."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%CONF_FILE%% is a file path; %%ADMIN_CONF_LINK%% is a documentation link; keep both exactly as written
#: help.md:125
msgid ""
"A local administrator can define a custom icon set by placing a "
"configuration file at %%CONF_FILE%%. An example with full documentation is "
"provided in %%ADMIN_CONF_LINK%%."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:132
msgid ""
"Most entries in this section have a tooltip with further details -- hover "
"over the label to read it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%TERMINAL_SIZE%% and %%SIZE_*%% are combo box labels in the settings; keep them exactly as written
#: help.md:143
msgid ""
"%%TERMINAL_SIZE%% -- size of the terminal window that opens during "
"upgrades. Options: %%SIZE_DEFAULT%% (2/3 of screen, capped at 960x600 on "
"wide displays), %%SIZE_ONE_THIRD%%, %%SIZE_HALF%%, %%SIZE_TWO_THIRDS%%, "
"%%SIZE_THREE_QUARTERS%%, %%SIZE_NINE_TENTHS%%, or %%SIZE_OWN%% (no size "
"hint -- the terminal uses its own saved size and position)."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%POSITION%% is the terminal position label; %%SIZE_OWN%% is a size combo box entry; keep them exactly as written
#: help.md:148
msgid ""
"%%POSITION%% -- screen position of the terminal window: center, top-left, "
"top-right, bottom-left, or bottom-right. Not available on Wayland or when "
"size is set to %%SIZE_OWN%%."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:151
msgid ""
"%%TERMINAL_AUTO_CLOSE%% -- close the terminal automatically after the "
"specified idle time once an upgrade completes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATOR: %%SKIP_UPGRADE_CONFIRMATION%% is a UI label; %%OPT_ASSUME_YES%% is a command-line option, do not translate it
#: help.md:156
msgid ""
"%%SKIP_UPGRADE_CONFIRMATION%% -- passes %%OPT_ASSUME_YES%% to apt or Nala, "
"automatically answering yes to the \"Do you want to continue?\" prompt. "
"Note: configuration questions from individual package scripts (debconf) may "
"still appear -- this is normal and not controlled by this setting. Use with "
"care: on a yes answer apt will proceed even if the upgrade would remove "
"packages to resolve a dependency conflict."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:159
msgid ""
"%%DESKTOP_NOTIFICATIONS%% -- show a desktop notification when updates "
"become available."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:162
msgid ""
"%%AUTOSTART_DELAY%% -- wait a short time after login before starting, so "
"the desktop is fully set up before MX Updater appears in the tray."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:165
msgid ""
"%%HIDE_WHEN_NO_UPDATES%% -- hide the tray icon when the system is up to "
"date. Not available on KDE/Plasma."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:167
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: help.md:169
msgid ""
"Authentication is required to upgrade packages. A password prompt will "
"appear."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:171
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: help.md:173
msgid "The tray icon does not appear"
msgstr ""

#: help.md:177
msgid ""
"MX Updater starts automatically at login via an XDG autostart entry "
"installed with the package. If the icon is missing it can be started "
"manually from %%MX_TOOLS%% or the %%SYSTEM_MENU%%. On some desktops the "
"system tray area must be added to the panel manually."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:181
msgid "A password is asked every time I click Upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: help.md:183
msgid "This is expected -- authentication is always required for upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: help.md:185
msgid "Updates are not detected"
msgstr ""

#: help.md:188
msgid ""
"Use %%CHECK_FOR_UPDATES%% from the right-click menu to force an immediate "
"check. The terminal window will show any errors, including a locked apt "
"database from another running package manager."
msgstr ""

